---
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Private client
    participant E as Entra ID / MI token service
    participant F as Foundry project API
    participant A as Hosted agent runtime
    participant R as Azure Resource Manager
    participant G as AI Gateway
    participant M as Foundry model
    participant O as Gateway monitoring

    Note over C,O: CURRENT private reference flow - verified October 25, 2026<br/>Entra to Foundry and ARM, API key from agent to gateway, gateway MI to model
    C->>E: Acquire Foundry token using client identity
    E-->>C: Foundry access token
    C->>F: Responses request through Foundry private endpoint<br/>Client token + project invocation permission
    F->>A: Dispatch to deployed agent version
    opt Runtime key cache needs refresh
        A->>E: Acquire ARM token using runtime managed identity
        E-->>A: ARM access token
        A->>R: Read default gateway key with scoped listSecrets permission
        R-->>A: Key retained only in runtime memory
    end
    A->>G: Prompt + gpt-mini + API key<br/>Injected agent subnet to gateway private endpoint
    G->>G: Validate key and apply configured token limit
    Note over A,G: Public gateway access stays disabled.<br/>Network access and authentication are independent.
    opt Gateway backend token needs refresh
        G->>E: Acquire model token using gateway managed identity
        E-->>G: Model-backend access token
    end
    G->>M: Model request with gateway identity token<br/>Gateway VNet integration to model private endpoint
    M-->>G: Model answer / HTTP 200
    G-)O: Export gateway and backend spans asynchronously
    G-->>A: HTTP 200 + model answer
    A-->>F: Agent response
    F-->>C: OK in the single live smoke test
    Note over G,O: Same trace contains gateway and model-backend HTTP 200.<br/>This does not establish agent-side telemetry delivery.
    Note over E,R: Token and key refresh can be cached.<br/>Entra and ARM connectivity are not depicted as private endpoints.
